@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5080/api/v1
# One request per endpoint. Every mutating call after login needs the cookie the login set and the
# csrf_token it returned in X-CSRF-Token. Run `urlog user create --db data/metadata.db --name alice --admin` first.
# The error paths: a wrong password is 401 with the same body as an unknown name; a 6th login attempt from one
# address inside a minute is 429 with Retry-After; a case the caller is not a member of is 404 on every route.

### Login (sets the urlog_session cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "alice", "password": "correct horse battery staple" }

### Who am I (also returns the CSRF token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Users (admin): list
GET {{baseUrl}}/users

### Users (admin): create
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "name": "bob", "password": "another long password", "role": "analyst" }

### Users (admin): one
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/2

### Users (admin): role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/2/role
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "role": "admin" }

### Users (admin): unlock early
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/2/unlock
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Users (admin): set a new password (ends the user's sessions)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/2/password
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "password": "yet another long password" }

### Cases: mine
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases

### Cases: create (the caller becomes owner)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "name": "incident 1" }

### Cases: one (404 unless a member)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1

### Cases: members
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/members

### Cases: share (owner)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/members
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "user": "bob", "role": "ro" }

### Cases: change a member's role (owner)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/members/2
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "role": "rw" }

### Cases: unshare (owner)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/members/2
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Admin: every case's metadata and members (never events)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases

### Admin: grant membership on any case (audited in the case's trail, by_admin: true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases/1/members
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "user": "alice", "role": "ro" }

### Admin: change a member's role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases/1/members/1
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "role": "rw" }

### Admin: remove a member
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/cases/1/members/1
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Upload: what the server speaks (tus 1.0: creation, termination, checksum, expiration)
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads

### Upload: create (owner or rw). Upload-Metadata is "key base64(value)" pairs: filename (required), host, timezone, year, nginx_log_format
POST {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads
Tus-Resumable: 1.0.0
Upload-Length: 11
Upload-Metadata: filename YWNjZXNzLmxvZw==,host d2ViLTAx
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

### Upload: how far it is (the id is the last segment of the Location the create answered).
### Urlog-Upload-State is the state; "finalising" with Upload-Offset = Upload-Length means all bytes are stored and the record is pending
HEAD {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads/{{upload}}
Tus-Resumable: 1.0.0

### Upload: a chunk at the current offset; the last one answers after intake has recorded the file.
### 503 with Retry-After: the bytes are stored and the metadata store is busy; the record follows, ask HEAD and send nothing again
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads/{{upload}}
Tus-Resumable: 1.0.0
Upload-Offset: 0
Content-Type: application/offset+octet-stream
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

hello world

### Upload: what became of it (state, offset, file id, SHA-256, job id)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads/{{upload}}

### Upload: give up an unfinished one
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/cases/1/uploads/{{upload}}
Tus-Resumable: 1.0.0
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}
